# Windows batch files MUST keep CRLF line endings. With LF only, cmd.exe
# mis-parses them - it chops the first characters off lines and the script
# fails in a confusing way rather than erroring cleanly. Checked out with CRLF
# on every platform so machine/sk.cmd survives a fresh clone.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
